# <type>[(<scope>)][!]: <imperative summary, 72 characters or fewer>
#
# Why is this change needed? What was wrong or missing before?
#
# What behavior or implementation changed? What user, configuration, or
# compatibility impact follows? Wrap prose at 72 characters.
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: <incompatible behavior and executable migration path>
# Fixes #<issue>
# Refs #<issue-or-pull-request>
#
# Header: <type>[(<scope>)][!]: <summary>
#
# Types: feat (feature), fix (bug fix), docs (documentation), test (tests),
# refactor (no behavior change), perf (performance), build (build/dependencies),
# ci (CI configuration), chore (maintenance), revert (revert a commit).
#
# Use a lowercase English type; use an imperative, lowercase English summary;
# do not add a period, emoji, WIP, fixup!, squash!, issue reference, or result.
# Add ! and BREAKING CHANGE: when changing public behavior incompatibly.
# Use only verified issue references and trailers; never fabricate validation,
# review, sign-off, authorship, or AI trailers.
